opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Generated OCaml bindings for the CometBFT ABCI protobuf types"
description: """
Protobuf types for the `tendermint.abci` package, generated with
ocaml-protoc-plugin from the .proto tree vendored at proto/ (pinned to CometBFT
v0.40.0).

The generated sources are committed to the repository, so building this package
does NOT require protoc or the ocaml-protoc-plugin binary. Run ./gen.sh to
regenerate them after bumping the vendored protos.

Depends only on base64 and ptime, and in particular NOT on unix, so it links
into a MirageOS/Solo5 unikernel.

The ocaml-protoc-plugin *runtime* is vendored under lib/proto/runtime rather
than depended on as a package: the package needs ppx_expect, ppx_inline_test,
omd and conf-protoc to build its code generator, and that cone defeats
opam-monorepo, which a unikernel build relies on. See lib/proto/runtime/README.md.
The plugin is still what generates the bindings -- it is just not a runtime
dependency.
"""
maintainer: ["gilbahat"]
authors: ["gilbahat"]
license: "ISC"
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft/issues"
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-cometbft.git"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "dune" {>= "3.0"}
  "base64" {>= "3.1.0"}
  "ptime"
]
build: [["dune" "build" "-p" name "-j" jobs]]

